      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Cosmic nihilism can be a sobering perspective, yet it fundamentally does not erase your personal meaningfulness or the love you hold for others. Even if the universe ends in heat death, the experiences you create matter deeply within the context of your own life and history. You do not need a grand cosmic purpose to find that your efforts, connections, and growth still have weight and significance here and now.",
